      "evidence_type": "published tag insertion at this exact site",
      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface display confirmed by NbALFA nanobody binding; normal expression reported. Transport function: NOT MEASURED in the cited ledger lines.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "Three ledger lines from PMC13454448 all describe the same SMVT_EM construct in which EL3 residues 484\u2013516 are replaced by the ALFA tag. The topology landmarks confirm that residues 477\u2013527 are extracellular (between TM10 at 456\u2013476 and TM11 at 528\u2013548), so residues 484\u2013516 lie entirely within this extracellular span. The paper's TM numbering (TM11/TM12) differs from the landmark numbering (TM10/TM11) but the residue coordinates are unambiguous. Python verification: seq[482]='M' (residue 483, residue_before) and seq[516]='T' (residue 517, residue_after). The tag replaces 484\u2013516, so insert_after_residue=483 places the ALFA tag between M483 and T517. Distance from residue 483 to the preceding TM boundary (476) = 7 residues (\u22653 \u2713); distance from residue 517 to the following TM boundary (528) = 11 residues (\u22653 \u2713). The GFP-fusion papers (PMC3230660, PMC5263180) describe 'hSMVT-GFP', a C-terminal fusion; the C-terminus (549\u2013635) is intracellular per the topology landmarks and therefore does not qualify as an extracellular tag site. Full-length SMVT construct (SMVT_EM) with the ALFA tag replacing EL3 residues 484\u2013516 was expressed in cells, bound by the NbALFA nanobody on the extracellular surface confirming surface display, and used for cryo-EM structural determination. The paper reports normal expression and proper NbALFA interaction. Transport function was not explicitly assayed in the cited ledger lines. [validation: surface_only; position: validated; source: paper; entailment_verified: True; position_repaired: true]",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 42364996,
          "citation": "PMID 42364996",
          "claim": "Specifically, we replaced the extracellular loop EL3 (residues 484-516) between TM11 and TM12 with a stable, short \u03b1-helix known as the ALFA tag (Fig. 1a )."
        }
      ],
